// Params read off the OBJ being traded, not off the shopkeeper - which is why they are not in
// shopkeeper.param.

// TRADEABLE BETWEEN PLAYERS, BUT NO SHOP WILL BUY IT. ~can_sell_obj already refuses an untradeable
// item everywhere, and that covers almost everything; what it did not cover is an item that is
// deliberately tradeable AND must not have a gp price, because five of this build's shops are
// allstock=yes and will buy literally anything.
//
// The vote ticket is the first of those. It has to be tradeable - selling your tickets instead of
// redeeming them is half the model - but a general store buying them would turn voting into a gp
// faucet at whatever cost= happened to say. A param rather than a hardcoded name in ~can_sell_obj
// (which is how the Al-Kharid silk rule is written) so the next such item needs no code.
[shop_will_not_buy]
type=boolean
default=no
